---
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout
  title="Before & After Studio Privacy Policy"
  description="How Before & After Studio handles local photos, projects, exports, Android sharing, and optional Google Play purchases."
>
  <article class="wrap prose">
    <p class="eyebrow">Privacy / Before & After Studio</p>
    <h1>
      Your photos.
      <br />
      <em>Your device.</em>
    </h1>
    <p class="intro">Before & After Studio Privacy Policy</p>
    <p>
      <strong>Effective date:</strong> November 5, 2026
      <br />
      <strong>Developer:</strong> Velvet & Pixel
      <br />
      <strong>Contact:</strong>{" "}
      <a href="mailto:velvetandpixel@gmail.com">velvetandpixel@gmail.com</a>
    </p>
    <h2>Photos and projects stay local</h2>
    <p>
      Before & After Studio edits photos on your Android device. We do not
      operate a photo upload server, cloud storage service, or user account
      system. We do not receive or collect your photos, project names, branding
      presets, or finished comparisons.
    </p>
    <p>
      When you select a photo or logo through Android’s system photo or document
      picker, the app copies it into private device storage. The original copy
      may contain metadata; the source file is not modified. Projects,
      thumbnails and presets are stored locally. The app does not request broad
      access to your photo library. A picker provider you choose may offer its
      own cloud features, governed by its own policies.
    </p>
    <h2>On-device editing, saving and sharing</h2>
    <p>
      Editing and rendering happen on your device. Finished JPEG and PNG exports
      do not include the original source GPS/EXIF metadata. Saving creates a
      separate image in your gallery or chosen location.
    </p>
    <p>
      Sharing sends the finished image to a destination you explicitly select
      through Android’s sharing controls. The receiving application’s privacy
      policy applies. Exported and shared copies are outside this app’s control
      and must be deleted separately.
    </p>
    <h2>Deleting your data</h2>
    <p>
      You can delete projects in the app. Deleting a project removes its managed
      original assets when no other project references them. Clearing the app’s
      storage or uninstalling it deletes local projects and settings. Android
      cloud backup and device transfer are disabled for app data.
    </p>
    <p>
      Save any finished images you want to keep before clearing storage or
      uninstalling. Images already exported to your gallery or another location
      remain there until you delete them. There is no app account or developer
      server-side photo data to delete.
    </p>
    <h2>Optional Google Play purchases</h2>
    <p>
      Pro is an optional one-time purchase processed by Google Play through your
      Google account. The app does not receive your payment card details. It
      stores signed purchase proof, a local purchase entitlement and the
      free-export allowance in private storage excluded from backup.
    </p>
    <p>
      The app verifies Google-signed purchase proof locally and uses Google Play
      to check and acknowledge purchases and restore ownership. Velvet & Pixel
      does not operate a purchase-verification server. Verified Pro access is
      cached for offline use. Purchases, restoration, current product prices and
      online ownership/refund checks require Google Play connectivity. A
      successful online refresh can update refunded or revoked ownership.
    </p>
    <p>
      Uninstalling or clearing storage removes the local purchase record and
      resets the local free allowance. Pro purchases can be restored using the
      Google Play account that owns the purchase.
    </p>
    <h2>Google services and SDKs</h2>
    <p>
      Google Play and associated Billing, Play services and diagnostic SDKs may
      process transaction, technical, device and operational diagnostic
      information under Google’s policies. These services use network access.
      Photos are not passed to the billing SDK. The absence of a
      developer-operated backend does not mean third-party services process no
      data.
    </p>
    <p>
      See{" "}
      <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy">Google’s Privacy Policy</a>{" "}
      and{" "}
      <a href="https://play.google.com/about/play-terms/">
        Google Play’s Terms of Service
      </a>{" "}
      for information about those services.
    </p>
    <h2>No developer-operated advertising or analytics</h2>
    <p>
      Velvet & Pixel does not operate advertising or analytics in Before & After
      Studio. The app has no advertisements or subscriptions.
    </p>
    <h2>Contact and policy updates</h2>
    <p>
      If you contact us by email, we receive the information you choose to send
      and use it to respond to your request. Please avoid sending private photos
      or payment details. Contact{" "}
      <a href="mailto:velvetandpixel@gmail.com">velvetandpixel@gmail.com</a>{" "}
      with privacy questions.
    </p>
    <p>
      Updates to this policy will be published at this URL with an updated
      effective date.
    </p>
  </article>
</Layout>
